# regression case 2: Stillinger lattice + periodic_xyz.  Exercises the
# SizeDistribution parser, the periodic image shifts in the cell list and the
# scaling compression path.
#
# NOTE: unlike the other two cases, this one is tied to the random number
# implementation.  Stillinger placement offsets each particle by
# 0.5*unif(eng)*dl and draws radii through a SizeDistribution, so the C++17
# migration (std::ranlux48_base replacing TR1's ranlux64_base_01) changed the
# realisation -- not the distribution: over 2e6 draws the two engines agree at
# mean 0.499999/0.500084 and sd 0.288646/0.288765 against a theoretical
# 0.5/0.2887.  If this case fails after an RNG change, check that before
# suspecting the physics.
boxsize		1 1 1
density		1
Gravity		0   0   0
outDt		0.01
timeStep	0.0001
maxTime		0.02
SizeDistribution uniform 0.5 0.5001
nParticle	200
stiffness	5e+02
damping		5e+0
friction	2.0e-1
output		out
method		Stillinger
boundary	periodic_xyz
eta		1.4
zeta		1.4
scaling		1.1
